---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import fishing2005 from '../assets/images/site/fishing_2005.jpeg';
import deer from '../assets/images/site/deer.png';
import ronan from '../assets/images/site/ronan_2.JPG';
import odin from '../assets/images/site/oden_dog_2.jpg';
---

<Base title="About" description="About Fisher Ankney.">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      Growing up in northern Michigan I was raised on a steady diet of hunting and fishing. My home town of
      Grayling boasts a rich outdoors heritage - it's where Fred Bear opened up shop in 1933 and 26 years later
      it's where Trout Unlimited was founded. Hell, even the ubiquitous Adam's fly was invented just a few miles
      down the road on the Boardman River.
    </p>
    <p>
      My parents had me out in the field back before I can remember, a service that I will forever be grateful
      for. We would regularly fly fish our favorite stretch of the Au Sable just ten or fifteen minutes from our
      house nearly year round.
    </p>
    <Image class="photo" src={fishing2005} alt="Fishing as a kid in 2005" width={720} />
    <p>
      November 15th is a holy day for all in Northern Michigan School would always be closed for this, the
      opening day of rifle season. I took my first whitetail with my bow from a tree stand in the woods behind
      the house at 13 and occasionally I still make the pilgrimage back to hunt whitetails in the north woods
      because there's nothing quiet like it.
    </p>
    <Image class="photo" src={deer} alt="Whitetails from the north woods in 2006 and 2023" width={720} />
    <p>
      On the day after I graduated high school I moved to Colorado, calling Fort Collins home for the next
      decade as I focused on getting an education and a career. Unfortunately I left most of my hunting and
      fishing behind during this time, only taking the occasional day trip to fish the overcroweded Poudre River.
      In early 2022 I decided I had enough of it and I moved to Boise - a city in a state to which I had never
      been before. Since the move I have been making the most out of every season in this bountiful new home.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="dogs">
    <article class="dog-card">
      <Image class="dog-photo" src={ronan} alt="Ronan, an Australian Shepherd" width={480} />
      <div class="dog-body">
        <h2>Ronan - Australian Shepard</h2>
        <p>
          I got Ronan from a random guy on Facebook looking to offload his now grown puppy because he "didn't
          have the time for him anymore" in January of 2021. Ronan was about a year old and unfortunately very
          poorly behaved. Our first six months were rough but we eventually established in him a good standard
          of canine citizenship. I am now happy to say that Ronan is my best buddy, his heart, devotion and
          personality makes up for the few stubborn behavioral shortcomings that remain.
        </p>
        <p>
          Ronan is at his best on the river, always faithfully watching over me from the bank or the back of
          the drift boat as I fish. He gives a mean bark and growl at anyone rude enough to low hole us -- and
          don't get him started on the rafters. Ronan loves to come hiking and camping, requiring very little
          supervision I often forget he's come along until he conspicuously steals all of the sticks from my
          firewood pile.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="dog-card">
      <Image class="dog-photo" src={odin} alt="Odin, a German Wirehaired Pointer puppy" width={480} />
      <div class="dog-body">
        <h2>Odin - German Wirehaired Pointer</h2>
        <p>
          Born March 5, 2025, little Odie my newest outdoor buddy. I'm planning to focus mainly on hunting the
          chukar hills and the snake with my new canine partner.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .photo {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-height: 420px;
    object-fit: cover;
    margin: 2rem auto;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  }

  .dogs {
    max-width: var(--content);
    margin: 3rem auto 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .dog-card {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  }

  .dog-photo {
    width: 100%;
    height: 200px;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }

  .dog-body h2 {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
  }

  .dog-body p {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    font-size: 1.075rem;
  }

  .dog-body p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .dog-card {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .dog-photo {
      height: 240px;
    }
  }
</style>
